THE DICTIONARY DATA IS NOT COVERED BY THE MIT LICENCE ABOVE.

The generated files under src/data carry the terms of the sources they were
built from. The MIT licence covers the code; these carry their own:

  src/data/core.ts, roget.ts, webster.ts, glossary.ts

* WordNet 3.0 - definitions, synonyms and antonyms.
  Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights reserved. Used under the
  WordNet licence, which permits use, copying, modification and distribution
  for any purpose, commercial or otherwise, provided its copyright notice and
  terms travel with any copy.

* Wiktionary - word origins and related words, via kaikki.org.
  Licensed CC BY-SA 3.0. Redistribution requires attribution and that
  derivative works of that content carry the same licence.

* Webster's Revised Unabridged Dictionary (1913) - public domain.
  This is the 1913 edition, not the modern Merriam-Webster dictionary, which
  is copyrighted and is not used here.

* Roget's Thesaurus (1911) - public domain.

* Google Web Trillion Word Corpus frequency ranks - open data, used only to
  decide which words are worth a card.

Anyone redistributing this project, or reusing the generated data files,
should carry these notices with them. The build scripts in scripts/ can
regenerate every one of those files from their sources.
